SUMMARY:Touch A Truck
DESCRIPTION:TOUCH A TRUCK\nFREE EVENT for all ages – no registration required! \nSaturday\, April 25\n10 am-Noon \nTouch A Truck puts kids in the driver’s seat! Join the Wilmette Park District\, Village of Wilmette and more during this FREE and unique opportunity to explore trucks of all types all in one place. Inspect the equipment\, meet the men and women who operate the big rigs and learn how they help us in our community. Attendees\, both young and young at heart are allowed to touch\, climb\, and ask questions about their favorite trucks in a safe\, supervised environment. \nTrucks may include buses\, plow trucks\, utility vehicles\, tractors\, loaders\, sweepers\, mowers\, fire and tow trucks\, pressure washers\, spray rigs\, and other service vehicles. \nSensory Friendly Start: 10-10:20 am\nPlease do not blow horns or honk the vehicles for the first 20 minutes of Touch A Truck to allow our noise-sensitive participants time to enjoy the event. \nThis event takes place in the parking lot of Centennial Recreation Center (2300 Old Glenview Road).  \n\nHave a truck or specialty vehicle you’d love to showcase? Vendors can email Julie Freels at jfreels@wilpark.org for participation information. \n\n  \n  Download PDF\n      \n          \n          \n           Save This Page as a PDF
URL:https://wilmettepark.org/event-list/touch-a-truck/
LOCATION:Centennial Parking Lot\, 2300 Old Glenview Road\, Wilmette\, 60091\, United States
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://d11ixze0kvt635.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/20164314/TAT26-Fi.jpg
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR